    "checklist.menu.moveCheckedItems" : {
      "comment" : "Overflow-menu entry on an existing checklist's detail screen. Moves the items the person has ticked into another checklist, picked on the sheet that opens next: they are added there and removed from this checklist. Keep the trailing ellipsis — it is what promises that sheet. It sits directly under the Copy Checked Items to… entry and must not read alike: that one leaves the items here, this one takes them away. Use the same word for checked items as that entry. \"to…\" means to a different checklist, never \"here\" or \"into this one\".",
